<!--Post: 4894--><!--Time: 1106797878-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4894"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 7:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The BTK will have been an EMS/T or RN during the times of the murders who had a penchant for wearing women&#39;s clothing at times and was a neat freak when it came to clutter and orderliness. <BR> <BR>Wouldn&#39;t we all freak out if he has had a sex change in the years since the murders and is now a &#34;woman&#34;?  He could drop stuff off all day and never be noticed...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4894-->
<!--Post: 4897--><!--Time: 1106799528-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4897"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK - Dressed To Kill!  I love it!  However, I&#39;m betting on BTK - Psycho...as in, &#34;He wouldn&#39;t hurt a fly.&#34;  More seriously, I will definitely go with neat freak, and I definitely go with him having a major lingerie fetish, including wearing.  I don&#39;t buy nurse, but admit it&#39;s possible.  I would DEFINITELY freak if he went under the knife - I just don&#39;t see him wanting to be anything other than the perfect BTK that he already is.  But it would be an absolute hoot.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4897-->
<!--Post: 4905--><!--Time: 1106800830-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4905"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I will go with him having a major lingerie fetish as well.   <BR>I will also go with the idea that his acts of murder are his rage at LE and or any form of control leaders in this world.  I think when he kills he is acting on a rage that he no longer recognizes as a rage. When he was killing he was no longer able to get in touch with himself when triggered by the MONSTER.   <BR>I think his silent and mysterious killings are his way of proving to himself that he can control those he sees as part of that group of persons who have had CONTROL over him for so long &#40;while maybe in military training or LE in his past..&#41;...Basically he has lost PART of his mind...but the other part works just fine.   <BR> <BR>As for guilt, sorrow in relation to any murder he committed, he does not have to feel those things when the NORMAL part of his mind remembers what he has done.  HE can blame that on the MONSTER he says caused him to do it.  He has apparently given his rage a name...and as long as he names it and blames it, he is not required to feel guilt or sorrow for what he has done.  JMO.. <BR>Thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4905-->
<!--Post: 5001--><!--Time: 1106847968-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5001"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 9:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Theory <BR> <BR>Feburary:  Two packages will be dropped off.  One may even be dropped off valentine&#39;s day.  They will both contain information about current victims, or any unknown victims.  He will alert the police by contacting different news and businness organizations.  The police will not release any details and continue to swab people, asking for help. <BR> <BR>March:  Either by the second Feb. drop off, or by March much of the pulic will be angered with the police.  Not to the point of rioting, no, but to the point where rants happen in bars, and online message boards decry them for keeping SO secretive that the case can&#39;t go much futher.  BTK will realize this, and realize that the police have been doing a fair job of keeping the attention off him ... he will mail the next letter to Tom Voigt or Charlie Otero directly, expecting that they would actually tell the public SOMETHING about himself.  Thus the public once again, greedily, submits to his fun and games and the case goes on. <BR> <BR>April:  Maybe one, or two dropoffs, sent to Voigt, Otero, and maybe even Bright or other victims. <BR> <BR>May:  Around this time the police will get the clue that BTK is not caring for them anymore, and realize the danger in that.  In order to get in control of the case they MUST KEEP BTK&#39;S ATTENTION ON THEM, and therefore they must keep the PUBLIC&#39;S attention on the police.  As long as the police are interesting, the public is interested, and when the public is interested then the BTK&#39;s sick mind plays games with the police and not with someone outside the case.  The Police will start releasing information that isn&#39;t vital to keep, while still keeping certain details silent.  I know its sickening to think that is how it works, but the BTK exsists only because we exsist to hear him.  The police need to realize that and in retrospect keep the Public interested.  The more clues BTK drops to satisfy himself and the public, the closer to BTK the police get. <BR> <BR>June:  A drop off, and between febuary and now I expect another murder to be revealed.  In all honestly I believe Delores Davis.   <BR> <BR>End of June to July:  BTK is caught.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5001-->
<!--Post: 5015--><!--Time: 1106849844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5015"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, my prediction hasn&#39;t changed, but I don&#39;t think WPD are that bad anymore.  Many of us are complaining about the lack of any useful information at that meeting too soon.  They&#39;ve had the evidence for ... what?   a day? <BR> <BR>Let the process it.  The police have done an okay job releasing information when necessary.  I just got tied up with the emotions of the case, mainly because everyone else is. <BR> <BR>Prediction doens&#39;t change though, because I don&#39;t expect most of the public to change their opinion ... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5015-->
<!--Post: 5106--><!--Time: 1106873618-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5106"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 4:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good thoughts Verm.  The pink colored crepe paper inside the Post Toastie box made me think immediatlely of Valentine Decoration.  I think you may have a good prediction here. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5106-->
